              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "17636255"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Induced under high salinity stress and stationary growth phase. Increased ectoine biosynthesis occurs as soon as the cells start to grow in high osmolality medium, but there is no immediate 5-hydroxyectoine production. Appreciable amounts of 5-hydroxyectoine are made only when cell growth slowed and the culture enters in stationary growth phase"
